From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:32:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, server: Take FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES to set a file's
 times and attributes, and keep attributes given as zero.

Setting FileBasicInformation needed no access right at all, and FileAttributes 0, which means "leave
them", cleared the hidden and system attributes and made a read-only file writable: SetFileTime()
sends it, so setting a hidden file's time showed it.  The fd cache now keeps FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES
next to the data rights, in the bit the file type did not use.

A read-only file could not be opened for FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES at all, as the server opened it for
Unix write; fchmod() and futimens() need no more than a read-only descriptor, so only truncating
still asks for one.  SetFileAttributesW() opens the file for FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES as Windows does.

The eighteen SetFileTime todos of kernel32's test_CreateFile pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

